      "id": "sl58644",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. WHAT IS A VERB?"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Verbs are broadly categorized into Finite vs Non-Finite verbs and Main vs Helping (Auxiliary) verbs.",
        "Primary auxiliaries include 'BE', 'HAVE', and 'DO', where 'DO' is heavily tested in SSC error detection.",
        "Modal verbs express specific moods and abilities, including pairings like CAN/COULD, MAY/MIGHT, and SHALL/WILL.",
        "Special semi-modals like NEED & DARE represent advanced grammar concepts frequently asked in exams.",
        "Applying the SSC Golden Rules is essential for correctly solving practice questions."
      ],
      "id": "3eb66x1"
    },
